# Why every setting, env var, header and command this gateway uses is here.
#
# The rule, from the published methodology: a setting may appear only if it is needed to boot the
# process at all, to point an upstream at the test mock instead of a real provider, to expose an
# ingress path the matrix exercises, or to bind the port and cores the rig requires. One claim per
# line: <pattern> <boot|upstream|ingress|bind>. Anything unclaimed is a lint failure, and a claim
# that matches nothing is a stale claim and also a failure.
#
# Migrated from GW_CONFIG_WHY in gateway.sh, which is dead code the lint was still reading.
deployment       boot      # the DB-less standalone block; without it APISIX demands an etcd cluster
role             boot
role_data_plane  boot
config_provider  boot      # routes from conf/apisix.yaml instead of etcd
apisix           bind
node_listen      bind      # the port the harness drives
nginx_config     bind
worker_processes bind      # nginx `auto` reads the HOST cpu count and is blind to --cpuset-cpus
routes    ingress   # the ai-proxy route table
id        ingress
uri       ingress   # one native ingress URI per dialect the matrix drives
methods   ingress
plugins   ingress
ai-proxy  ingress
provider       upstream  # which provider dialect this route egresses in
options        upstream  # the model id sent upstream in that dialect
override       upstream  # -> the mock host, keeping the provider's native upstream path
auth           boot      # ai-proxy's schema REQUIRES an auth block; a route without one is dropped
provider_conf  boot      # bedrock: region, required by validate_provider_requirements
aws            boot      # bedrock: SigV4 material, required by the schema (dummy; mock ignores it)
access_key_id      boot
secret_access_key  boot

x-bench-egress ingress # Selects the supported Anthropic-to-OpenAI converter on the shared Messages ingress path
priority ingress # Header-qualified conversion route must precede the native Anthropic fallback

Five pairs passed local protocol response and upstream-recorder checks. The pinned converter registry contains Anthropic Messages to OpenAI Chat and an unrelated embeddings conversion; no other chat translation is claimed. Gemini and Vertex provider names here describe OpenAI-compatible service endpoints, not native Gemini wire support.
